# KaminIDE patches — gpui-pre-windows 0.3.8 (zed 279fe070bb389b79652e52065b2f001edcc0b11b)
#
# 1. Adapter policy: instance-owned typed DXGI preference, unchanged default enumeration, device recovery and live adapter LUID/driver identity.
# 2. DirectWrite: CSS font selection, shaping, vertical glyphs and fallback metrics.
# 3. DirectX: CSS primitives, images, filters, masks, gradients and per-window frame readback with copy/map duration delivered to the explicit host endpoint.
# 4. Window lifecycle: per-window rendering/resize policy and deterministic WPT scale.
# 5. Process shutdown: drain deferred native window destruction, stop and join owned vsync threads while pumping messages, then release GPU/text devices before leaving the platform loop.
# 6. Diagnostics: application-owned GPU batch measurements and typed startup configuration survive device recovery; environment parsing belongs to the host.
# 7. Tests: initialize unfragmented backdrop fixtures against the paired GPUI surface fields.
# 8. Unsafe invariants: added unsafe blocks are windows-rs COM/Win32 calls on interfaces owned by the live DirectX/DirectWrite state, called on the thread that owns that state, with HRESULTs and out-parameters checked before use. Raw memory is touched in three places only: the frame-capture readback copies w*4 bytes per row of a w x h BGRA8 staging texture between Map and Unmap (RowPitch >= w*4), GPU timing reads a query result through the raw GetData vtable entry into a plain-data out-value whose size is passed with it, and external-texture registration adopts a non-null ID3D11Texture2D pointer already AddRef'd by the caller (from_raw takes that reference). Release builds never select the debug-only WARP/D3D11On12 device overrides.
